WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.160 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
Before interpreting the root’s numbers,

2
00:00:02.360 --> 00:00:04.960 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
check which calculation mode produced them.

3
00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:08.660 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
Independent scalar bounds
summarize each property separately.

4
00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:13.140 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
Coherent scenario analysis keeps the
values belonging to one achievable

5
00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:14.900 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
attack alternative together.

6
00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:18.160 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
Those interpretations answer
different questions about the

7
00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:19.480 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
same FireSat tree.

8
00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:23.920 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
For example, one alternative may be
cheap but produce little attacker

9
00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:27.760 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
benefit, while another costs
more and offers a greater reward.

10
00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:32.140 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
Selecting the cheapest cost and
largest benefit independently does not

11
00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:34.160 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
create a real combined alternative.

12
00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:38.840 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
Read scalar bounds as bounds,
not as one complete attack story.

13
00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:42.280 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
Open Metric rules and expand Actor, victim,

14
00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:44.660 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
utilities and opportunity configuration.

15
00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:50.260 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
The Analysis profile JSON records the
mode, scenario budget, utility curves,

16
00:00:50.260 --> 00:00:51.720 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
and opportunity assumptions.

17
00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:56.660 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
Here we use a prepared training profile;
review its units and assumptions,

18
00:00:56.940 --> 00:00:59.000 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
then choose Stage rules if you change it.

19
00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:02.380 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
Inspect the root and its
selected scenario identifier.

20
00:01:02.740 --> 00:01:07.680 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
Scenario mode preserves whole OR
alternatives and combines the required AND

21
00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:09.340 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
or ordered SAND actions.

22
00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:14.300 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
Derived feasibility, propensity, and
risk depend on the configured actor,

23
00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:18.420 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
victim, and opportunity model; they
are not interchangeable with the

24
00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:20.040 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
underlying raw effort inputs.

25
00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:22.860 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
Open Validation and examine the findings.

26
00:01:23.380 --> 00:01:26.440 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
Unknown inputs, unsupported
shared-event correlations,

27
00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:30.320 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
and exhausted scenario budgets
can make analysis incomplete.

28
00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:33.080 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
A failed threshold is a different finding.

29
00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:37.160 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
Never present a partial maximum
as the established worst case,

30
00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:39.780 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
or mistake the number of
displayed routes for the number

31
00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:41.080 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
of complete scenarios.

32
00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:45.440 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
At the upper right of the canvas,
select Nocturne for dark mode,

33
00:01:45.780 --> 00:01:47.140 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
then Parchment to return.

34
00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:49.440 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
This changes presentation only.
